{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_1",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "How does the SARS-CoV-2 reinfection rate change over time? The global evidence from systematic review and meta-analysis",
      "reason": "The title explicitly identifies the report as a systematic review (and meta-analysis)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "How does the SARS-CoV-2 reinfection rate change over time? The global evidence from systematic review and meta-analysis",
      "reason": "The title conveys the main objective/review question: the change in SARS-CoV-2 reinfection rate over time, at the global level."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "The global evidence from systematic review and meta-analysis",
      "reason": "The title provides supplementary information on the analysis method (meta-analysis) and scope (global evidence)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 95
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "There is a significant increase in the number of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection reports in various countries. However, the trend of reinfection rate over time is not clear.",
      "reason": "The abstract background describes the current state of knowledge (increasing reinfection reports) and explicitly identifies the key uncertainty (unclear trend of reinfection rate over time); the Introduction (text_4) further describes the global burden and ongoing mutation of SARS-CoV-2."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "The results of this study could help guide public health measures and vaccination strategies in response to the Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) pandemic.",
      "reason": "The need for the review is explained: the unclear time trend of reinfection motivates the meta-analysis, and the Introduction (text_4) emphasizes that SARS-CoV-2 'remains a global health threat,' establishing the review's importance."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_15",
      "quote": "the advantage of this study was that compared with the previous meta-analysis of the SARSCoV-2 reinfection rate, first, to avoid the heterogeneous impact of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection definition on SARSCoV-2 reinfection rates",
      "reason": "The Discussion acknowledges a previous meta-analysis and explains how the current review improves on it, but the previous review is not identified or cited, and this comparison is not made in the Introduction/rationale section."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a review of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection rates (etiology/prognosis), not a review of intervention effects, so no mechanism of action needs to be described."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review does not evaluate complex interventions or delivery contexts, so a logic model is not required."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 82
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_4",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "Therefore, the aim of this study was to conduct a meta-analysis to describe and summarize the current reinfection rates in different regions and among diverse populations. Furthermore, the study sought to examine trends in reinfection rates over time, so as to provide reference for the development of global unified reinfection standards and reinfection measures in the future.",
      "reason": "The objectives are explicitly stated: to meta-analyze current SARS-CoV-2 reinfection rates across regions/populations and to examine time trends in reinfection rates. The title also frames the review question ('How does the SARS-CoV-2 reinfection rate change over time?')."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a review of reinfection rates (frequency estimation) with meta-regression, not a review of intervention effects comparing interventions, so PICO-formatted planned comparisons do not apply."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "The inclusion criteria were: (1) Conformed to research questions, i.e., studies that estimated the reinfection rate of SARS-CoV-2 or we could calculate it based on the data provided in the paper; (2) The study design included cohort study, case-control study, and descriptive study; (3) The study fited our working definition of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection... reinfection working definition in this study was based on a positive laboratory result at least 90 days after laboratory confirmation of primary infection",
      "reason": "Eligible study designs, the research question (reinfection rate estimation), and the reinfection working definition (≥90 days between positive tests) are explicitly specified."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "To avoid language bias, the search was not limited to any language... The exclusion criteria were: ... (4) Grey literature, including a range of documents not controlled by commercial publishing organizations.",
      "reason": "Language (no restriction) and publication status (grey literature excluded) are reported, but dissemination year limits are not specified."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "One of them reported only the reinfection rate, but not the associated number of first infections as well as the number of reinfections... Therefore, we excluded the above literature with the number of unreported infections",
      "reason": "The review does not explicitly distinguish exclusion because outcomes were not measured from exclusion because outcome results were not reported; the exclusion reason given conflates data reporting with eligibility."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "Subgroup analyses were performed for age, reinfection variant, country, study population, and study type respectively",
      "reason": "Groups used in the syntheses (age, variant, country, population, study type) are specified and correspond to the review objective of describing reinfection rates across regions and populations and over time."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_19",
      "quote": "first, we did not include the 'grey literature', which may lack potential relevant studies that meet the inclusion criteria [35]... In order to avoid data heterogeneity in metaanalysis while ensuring data quantity, we used previous literature and previous definitions of reinfection in some countries as the criteria for included literature",
      "reason": "Rationales for notable restrictions (excluding grey literature; adopting the 90-day reinfection definition to limit heterogeneity) are provided."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 88
}

